  <!--
    REV_FinanceOnly - the second column security profile TAD section 6.1 names ("restricts
    all Bank Account and Payment columns to the Finance role"). Built under WBS 0.4's
    remainder, now that rev_bankaccount and rev_payment exist (see the header note above this
    element's sibling profile for the corrected history).

    WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT DO - same shape as REV_TrusteeRestricted above: this element
    grants Allowed (4) on every operation for every one of the 16 IsSecured=1 columns across
    rev_bankaccount (7) and rev_payment (9). rev_bankaccount.rev_name and rev_payment.rev_name
    - each table's primary name attribute - are deliberately absent: Dataverse does not permit
    field-level security on a primary name (0x8004f501, ground-truthed 2026-08-23 against a live
    ensure-schema.ps1 run against DEV; see each table's own Entity.xml header for the full
    story). The earlier count here (18: 8 + 10) included both name columns as IsSecured=1
    before that run proved the platform rejects it - corrected in place rather than silently,
    per this project's own convention. The control is not in what it grants - it is in
    who is a MEMBER, which is per-environment state applied by
    provisioning/dataverse/ensure-column-security-profile-members.ps1, not a solution
    component (TAD section 6, 6.1, 6.2; NFR-002). Per TAD section 6.2's own role table, the
    intended membership is the REV Finance role's group team only - REV Admin is deliberately
    NOT a member, the same way REV Trustee is deliberately not a member of the sibling profile,
    because NFR-002 / separation of duties requires bank details to sit behind one role and one
    role only. REV Admin already carries no TABLE privilege on either table (see Roles/REV
    Admin/REV Admin.xml); this profile is the second, independent layer of the same control at
    the column level, so even a future table-privilege mistake on REV Admin would still not
    expose these columns to it.

    EVERY IsSecured=1 COLUMN ON rev_bankaccount AND rev_payment MUST APPEAR BELOW, AND NOTHING
    ELSE SHOULD - same rule and same verification method as the sibling profile:
    `scripts/verify-field-security-coverage.py` checks both directions mechanically. Confirmed
    2026-08-23 against data-agent's own Entity.xml for both tables, AFTER the primary-name
    correction below: exactly 16 columns carry IsSecured=1, and all 16 are listed below - 7 on
    rev_bankaccount (rev_accountholdername, rev_sortcode, rev_accountnumber, rev_active,
    rev_applicantid, rev_providerid, rev_payeetype - rev_name excluded, see above) and 9 on
    rev_payment (rev_grantid, rev_bankaccountid, rev_providerid, rev_amount, rev_paymentdate,
    rev_method, rev_qboreference, rev_isfinalpayment, rev_paymentstatus - rev_name excluded,
    see above).

    fieldsecurityprofileid BELOW IS THE REAL, GROUND-TRUTHED id (C-TECH-051) - no longer a
    sentinel. The reviewer ran `provisioning/dataverse/ensure-schema.ps1 -Env dev` by hand on
    2026-08-23 (this session's own permission classifier refuses that live write) and confirmed
    the profile was created in DEV; the id below was read back live via
    `fieldsecurityprofiles?$filter=name eq 'REV_FinanceOnly'&$select=fieldsecurityprofileid` and
    substituted here and in the matching `<RootComponent type="70" .../>` in Other/Solution.xml,
    exactly as REV_TrusteeRestricted's own id was fixed on 2026-08-14 and REV Trustee's role id
    was fixed on 2026-08-21. A-FIN-03 in the Dev Summary's Unvalidated Assumptions Register is
    closed VERIFIED on this evidence.
  -->
  <FieldSecurityProfile name="REV_FinanceOnly" description="Releases the 16 Tier 4 Bank Account and Payment columns to the Finance role only. Every persona that is not a member of this profile - including REV Admin, REV Service Automation and REV Trustee - receives no value for these columns from any surface: app, view, export or API." fieldsecurityprofileid="{93d339bc-289f-f111-b8de-7ced8d43e87d}">
    <FieldPermissions>
      <!-- rev_bankaccount.rev_name is NOT listed here, deliberately. It is the table's primary
           name attribute, and Dataverse does not permit field-level security on a primary name
           (0x8004f501, ground-truthed 2026-08-23 against a live ensure-schema.ps1 run - see
           Entities/rev_bankaccount/Entity.xml's own header). A field permission cannot target an
           unsecured column, so there is no entry for it. -->
      <FieldPermission>
        <!-- The name on the account - a provider's business name or, for a reimbursement, the applicant's own name. Financial and, in the applicant case, personal data. -->
        <EntityName>rev_bankaccount</EntityName>
        <AttributeName>rev_accountholdername</AttributeName>
        <CanRead>4</CanRead>
        <CanUpdate>4</CanUpdate>
        <CanCreate>4</CanCreate>
        <CanReadUnmasked>0</CanReadUnmasked>
      </FieldPermission>
      <FieldPermission>
        <!-- The UK bank sort code. Financial identifier. -->
        <EntityName>rev_bankaccount</EntityName>
        <AttributeName>rev_sortcode</AttributeName>
        <CanRead>4</CanRead>
        <CanUpdate>4</CanUpdate>
        <CanCreate>4</CanCreate>
        <CanReadUnmasked>0</CanReadUnmasked>
      </FieldPermission>
      <FieldPermission>
